## Commands
```bash
npm run dev        # dev server (localhost:3000)
npm run build      # production build
npm run typecheck  # TypeScript check without emit
npm test           # run test suite
vercel --prod      # deploy to production (ask before running)
```

## Conventions
<!-- Your project's rules — Claude will follow these -->
- TypeScript strict mode
- Functional React components only
- Tailwind for all styling — no CSS modules
- Server components by default; add 'use client' only when needed
- Use `supabaseAdmin` for server writes, `supabase` for reads

## Environment variables
```
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=
```

## Do not
- Commit secrets or API keys
- Run `vercel --prod` without explicit approval
- Modify the DB schema without updating `supabase/schema.sql`
- Add `use client` to components that don't need it
